  "negative_controls_and_interpretation": {
    "31x31": "R4 selector chose JANUS GF2 and achieved 3.351x to 3.989x speedup over fastest *verified external* competitor on both Ubuntu host jobs, same formula, original SAT model fully validated.",
    "43x43_two_seeds": "R4 abstained from own GF2, choosing CMS native XOR with near-zero regret vs external controls. The diagnostic own GF2 was about 3x faster, but its speedup is NOT a win for the frozen R4 selector.",
    "width5_random_XOR": "R4 correctly refused out-of-training-family GF2 but plain original-CNF CMS was much slower than certified-native-XOR CMS and diagnostic JANUS GF2. Demonstrates important cross-family generalization failure; do not reclassify R4 as a win.",
    "partial_XOR_and_3SAT": "R4 refused unsafe own GF2 on incomplete/non-XOR sources; original-CNF selected outputs all SAT-verified, but partial XOR incurred 28–32% regret against CaDiCaL.",
    "13x13": "R4 selected native XOR, small under-10% regret relative to external fastest on both hosts.",
    "all_censoring": "Any timeout is treated as unverified and never given a numerical solve-time win.",
    "next_hypothesis_only": "Research R5 must learn structural classes of non-grid exact XOR and perhaps safer fallback SAT selection from R4 TRAINING observations; R4 test data cannot be reused as a sealed R5 evaluation."
